---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import households from "../data/households.json";
---
<Base title="The households">
  <h1>The households</h1>
  <p class="lede">Three reconstructed families of the parish of Sant'Andrea at Arienzo, covering the years
  1759 to 1869 — read out of the parish registers entry by entry.</p>

  {households.map(h => (
    <section style="margin:2rem 0">
      <h2 style="margin-top:1rem">{h.name}</h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Person</th><th>Event</th><th>Date</th><th>What the register says</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{h.members.map(m => (
          <tr>
            <td><strong>{m.person}</strong><br/><span class="small">{m.role}</span></td>
            <td>{m.event}</td>
            <td class="mono">{m.date}</td>
            <td><em>{m.evidence}</em>{m.ark ? <><br/><span class="mono small">{m.ark}</span></> : null}</td>
          </tr>))}</tbody>
      </table></div>
    </section>
  ))}

  <h2>What these three tables establish</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The line reaches a generation further back than it did.</strong> Pasquale Falco's own
    baptism of 24 October 1767 names his father <strong>Matteo Falco</strong> and his mother
    <strong>Francesca Crisci</strong>. Matteo replaces the unproven Agostino Falcone.</li>
    <li><strong>Vincenzo's marriage names four people at once</strong> — himself, his father Pasquale, his
    mother Chiara Rivetti, and his wife Andreana's father Arcangelo Crisci. It is the single most
    load-bearing document found.</li>
    <li><strong>The Crisci marry in twice.</strong> Matteo Falco married a Crisci in the 1760s; his
    great-grandson Vincenzo married another, Andreana, two generations later. Anna Falco — Pasquale's
    daughter — married an Arcangelo Crisci and died at 22 in 1820.</li>
    <li><strong>Children die.</strong> Maria Angela, baptised February 1802, was buried in March 1805
    aged about three. Giovanna was buried the same year. The name Maria was given twice, in 1789 and
    again in 1790 — the ordinary arithmetic of an 18th-century parish.</li>
    <li><strong>The same women recur.</strong> <em>Cecilia Martone</em> appears as midwife or godmother
    across some twenty years of these registers; <em>Gelsumina Ruggiero</em> stands godmother to
    Vincenzo's children. A parish is a small number of people doing the same offices for one another.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
